-- facts/ast-within-readers.rofl — WHO READS THE ANCESTOR RELATION, AND WHAT THEY ASK OF THE TREE.
--
-- Every premise of rules/js-*.rofl that reads ast_within (the strict ancestor relation) or ast_in
-- (parent/child), classified for w_data_structures (f_a_structure_is_declared_and_does_not_change_the_meaning):
-- a declared `tree` is worth the operations it answers, so the readers decide which operations.
-- Taken at 54a4be1 by reading each rule in written order; the frozen copy examples/linter/corpus-dataflow.rofl
-- (rules/js-dataflow.rofl at 4f997a6) and the planted fixture examples/shapes/fixture.rofl are not counted.
-- Read in a world by examples/checks/ast-within-readers-check.rofl.
--
--   reader(Site, File, Question, Pattern)   one premise; Site is Head_Line_N, N counting the
--                                           ast_within/ast_in premises of that clause
--   reader_head(Site, Head, Line)           the clause: its head relation, the line it starts on
--   reader_reads(Site, Rel)                 ast_within or ast_in
--   reader_note(Site, Text)                 what the premise means in the rule
--
-- Pattern is the arguments bound WHEN THE PREMISE IS REACHED in written order, ancestor (parent)
-- first: bb both bound, bf ancestor bound and descendant free, fb descendant bound and ancestor free,
-- ff neither.
--
-- Question, closed:
--   is_ancestor            both ends bound: a test
--   ancestors_of           descendant bound: the ancestors, a filter on them in later premises
--   descendants_of         ancestor bound: the subtree, a filter on it in later premises
--   scoped_ascent          ancestors of a node up to a boundary the next premise names (the path between)
--   scoped_descent         the subtree stopping at a boundary (a function), as a recursive walk over ast_in
--   nearest_with_property  the first ancestor with a property, as a recursive walk up over ast_in
--   children_of            ast_in with the parent bound (the seed of a walk)
--   parent_of              ast_in with the child bound (the seed of a walk)
--   depth, subtree_count, other   asked by no reader (the census says so)

edb(reader).
edb(reader_head).
edb(reader_reads).
edb(reader_note).


reader(in_own_decorator_254_1, "rules/js-callgraph.rofl", descendants_of, bf).
reader_head(in_own_decorator_254_1, in_own_decorator, 254).
reader_reads(in_own_decorator_254_1, ast_within).
reader_note(in_own_decorator_254_1, "the nodes under a decorator").

